(DBMS Normalization - Sample Notes) Tj T*
(Normalization organizes relational tables to reduce redundancy and update anomalies.) Tj T*
(First Normal Form \(1NF\): each column contains atomic values and rows are unique.) Tj T*
(Second Normal Form \(2NF\): a table in 1NF has no partial dependency on a composite key.) Tj T*
(Third Normal Form \(3NF\): a table in 2NF has no transitive dependency of a non-key attribute.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
